•fauthorxApub:sha2-256:ks7g2ycpdnhjdtsn3sfoiqoh2tazwtiwr2emxut3ugourttnnbkadbodyßeclassharchivalgcontentxqpubkit 0.19.0 was released on 2026-10-29 from commit a216bfc1d627b964d5bebed8ab4f4b12d3d7ffbe with these changes.ddata¢gcolumnsÇ°dnamehcategory°dnamefchangedrowsÜÇgchangedy:pubkit's main ruleset merges through GitHub's merge queue (merge commits, one group of up to five at a time) instead of requiring a branch to be up to date with main: the queue runs the required checks on the pull request merged into main as main will hold it, so the tree the checks passed is still the tree main holds after the merge and tagging a release needs no tests of its own, and pull requests stacked behind one another merge one at a time without anyone updating a branch. GitHub offers a merge queue only to an organization's public repositories, so a repository without one says "queue": false in its protected.json entry or pubkit.json protect block, or `pubkit protect --no-queue`, and keeps requiring an up-to-date branch. `pubkit protect --check` and the board report a repository whose ruleset does not matchÇgchangedy8The pull request workflow pubkit sync writes (pr.yml) also runs on merge_group, the merge queue's run of a pull request, so ci / passed and release / release report on the queue's merge and a queued pull request can merge. pubrel's release workflow only reports the check there: it tags from a push to main aloneÇhinternalxßpubkit's own CI runs on merge_group too, so its required checks report in the merge queue; the release tags and the wheel is built from a push to main alone, as beforeÇefixedxùpubkit cache run no longer fails when a rule entry, or a unit value filling one, names files outside the repository: each file is named relative to its entryÇefixedyïpubkit bump, the nightly's pubkit pins, pubkit sync --check and pubkit conform cover every use of pubkit at a release in a repository's workflows, generated or hand-written: its reusable workflows (such as a hand-written ci.yml calling service-ci.yml or rust-ci.yml) as well as its actions. 0.18.0 moved and checked only the actions, so a hand-written service-ci.yml pin stayed at the old pubkit unnoticedÇgchangedy–The cache block is one map of named entries, each taking path (was dir), refresh (run, day, week, month or never), version, inputs (were unit and shared file entries), tools (were tool: entries) and unit (one pattern with {unit}; pubkit cache run takes --unit VALUE); an entry needs refresh or inputs, an unknown key fails pubkit sync naming it, each entry gets its own cache key, and actions/cache's save prunes, so pubkit cache prune is no longer a workflow stepgdependsÅxApub:sha2-256:lrndjz3ob2swsyfjhzf2qcd3szfxnrpv6ayifsgphuvxy53u5tnqhevidenceÅ§dkindhexternalcreffpubkithrevisionx(a216bfc1d627b964d5bebed8ab4f4b12d3d7ffbedrolefsourcedlangbenescope¢jconditionsÄfdomainx'the published release v0.19.0 of pubkitgcreatedt2026-10-29T00:00:00Zcpuba1dtypekclaim.prose